      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14190078/assets/9c18d92044cb10ba7096ff66c14a27b3972fce71ef682e595bfda6fe17d3627d.png)\n\nUsing the graphical method, find the solutions $(x,y)$ of the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=5 \\\\ y=9-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The solutions $(x,y)$ of the system correspond to the intersection points of the two curves.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14190078/assets/6cc1ff4616ee97503866364c36adf18d1c8aa0f275f76ab4abe6ae63f014cec8.png)\n\nFrom the graph, the curves intersect at \n\n$\\,$ $(-2,5)\\,$ and $\\,(2,5).$ \n\nTherefore, these are the solutions of the corresponding system.",
