      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14190078/assets/96b7c8e8f6d1203327271f4960bde8804315f0f4ac6846beeb4a248af8b07b1a.png)\n\nUsing the graphical method, find the solutions $(x,y)$ of the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=x-1 \\\\ y={x}^{2}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The solutions $(x,y)$ of the system correspond to the intersection points of the two curves.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14190078/assets/82ec1e7cdbe6275bc4fac3cdf32e07eb989570d82b66bb5a980f25355293e3f9.png)\n\nFrom the graph, the curves intersect at \n\n$\\,$ $(-1,-2)\\,$ and $\\,(2,1).$ \n\nTherefore, these are the solutions of the corresponding system.",
